MySQL plugin SDK for MySQL @MYSQL_NO_DASH_VERSION@

These are the server's own headers, as they were when this server was
built. They are installed so that plugins, loadable functions and
components can be built without the server source tree. They make no
compatibility promise beyond what the server checks when it loads an
extension.

Storage engine, daemon and information schema plugins are version locked.
One built against this SDK loads only into a server of exactly this
version, with the same compatibility key, which the server reports as
@@build_compat_key.

Other plugin kinds, loadable functions and components are checked against
their own interface versions, and may load into other releases whose
interfaces match.

The compile and link flags this SDK records are part of the ABI. Build
with them, as MYSQL_SDK_ADD_PLUGIN in the MySQLSDK CMake package does.
